Datanaut-AB Database Trigger Summary

This file summarizes the six T-SQL triggers implemented on the Project Management database to enforce data integrity and track changes.


TR_Project_ArchiveStatus:

    Function: Automatically sets the ProjectEndDate to the current system time (GETDATE()) when the ProjectStatus is changed to 'Archived' for the first time.
    
    Purpose: Ensures archived projects have an accurate closing timestamp.

TR_Project_DateValidation:
  
    Function: Prevents INSERT or UPDATE operations if the ProjectEndDate is before the ProjectStartDate.
    
    Purpose: Enforces chronological integrity of project timelines.

TR_Project_BudgetValidation:

    Function: Prevents INSERT or UPDATE operations if the Budget value is negative.
    
    Purpose: Enforces the business constraint that a budget must be non-negative.

TR_TimeLogging_ProjectStatus:
  
    Function: Prevents logging new time entries (via the TimeLogging table) if the associated Project's status is 'Completed' or 'Archived'.
    
    Purpose: Enforces project closure and prevents activity against finished work. (Achieved by joining TimeLogging -> Report -> Project)

TR_UsingResourceAllocation_ProjectStatus:

    Function: Attempts to prevent resource allocation if the related employee is assigned to a 'Completed' or 'Archived' project.
    
    Purpose: Resource control. (Note: This logic is overly broad and should ideally link the resource use directly to a specific project ID.)

TR_Changes_Project (Audit Trail):

    Function: Logs all INSERT, UPDATE, and DELETE operations on the Project table into the Project_AuditLog table.
    
    Purpose: Provides a complete, future-proof history of all changes, capturing old and new row states as JSON objects for easy retrieval and maintenance.
